# kills: SG: N-A7 the crowded 24-note pan: the real SMALL_LABELS warning (two lines) opens Edit, a tapped anchor raises the notice, the warning yields and the three-row seed box stays readable at every keyboard
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^SG:.N-A7.the.crowded tests/e2e.test.js
# A pan warning no longer steps aside for a standing notice, so a two-line SMALL_LABELS warning plus the notice grows the slot and the seed box is clipped under the keyboard.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -958,7 +958,6 @@ footer.seq{row-gap:var(--sp-1)}
    The aria-live copy of the warning (.announce) is a separate element and still speaks. The class is on
    #scale-sheet, not the wrapper: paintLayout() reaches the sheet through a variable the sandbox already
    has, and say() rewrites #scale-msg's own className on every call, which also clears .pan. */
-#scale-sheet.noticed #scale-msg.warn.pan{display:none}
 /* The footer lip: open, the wrappers generate no box, so the footer is the layout it always was. */
 #scale-foot, #scale-footclip, #scale-footslide{display:contents}
 #scale-lip[hidden]{display:none}
